        {
          "id": "6c15ad25-7e65-364d-be34-28af3cb22c26",
          "content": {
            "id": "6c15ad25-7e65-364d-be34-28af3cb22c26",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Ryanair lifts fare growth forecast on strong early 2026 bookings",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Ryanair on Monday (January 26) boosted its forecast for average fare growth.\u00a0</p><p>That's after bookings for 2026 got off to a strong start.</p><p>And the firm predicted annual after-tax profit would likely jump by a third.</p><p>Europe's largest airline by passenger numbers said average fares would be 1 or 2 percentage points higher for the year to March\u00a0than the 7% annual growth it forecast in November.</p><p>The Irish airline said it's \"cautiously guiding\" after-tax profit to land between $2.5 billion and $2.7 billion.</p><p>Ryanair earned an after-tax profit of $136 million in the final three months of 2025.</p><p>That was excluding an exceptional $100 million charge related to a fine from the Italian competition authority in December.</p><p>Chief Executive Michael O'Leary said in a video statement that he was confident the full fine would be overturned on appeal.</p><p>Although he added that it could take a year or two.</p><p>Ryanair has been forced to cut capacity growth in recent years due to delays at Boeing.</p><p>But it said relations with the U.S. firm are now going well.\u00a0</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Ryanair on Monday (January 26) boosted its forecast for average fare growth.&nbsp;</p><p>That's after bookings for 2026 got off to a strong start.</p><p>And the firm predicted annual after-tax profit would likely jump by a third.</p><p>Europe's largest airline by passenger numbers said average fares would be 1 or 2 percentage points higher for the year to March&nbsp;than the 7% annual growth it forecast in November.</p><p>The Irish airline said it's \"cautiously guiding\" after-tax profit to land between $2.5 billion and $2.7 billion.</p><p>Ryanair earned an after-tax profit of $136 million in the final three months of 2025.</p><p>That was excluding an exceptional $100 million charge related to a fine from the Italian competition authority in December.</p><p>Chief Executive Michael O'Leary said in a video statement that he was confident the full fine would be overturned on appeal.</p><p>Although he added that it could take a year or two.</p><p>Ryanair has been forced to cut capacity growth in recent years due to delays at Boeing.</p><p>But it said relations with the U.S. firm are now going well.&nbsp;</p></body>",
